---
// How the planner's numbers work (static; ships no JavaScript).
---

<section class="planner-notes" aria-label="About the numbers">
  <p>
    <b>How the numbers work.</b> Every value comes from the game files: each vehicle's base configs, plus the exact tuning each upgrade,
    trait, part and ability applies. The game's own operations are combined as (base + adds + base × percentage adds) × multipliers.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>"of default"</b> means the base value isn't set in any data file (it's a code default), so only the change is shown. Curves are speed-
    or angle-based response tables; expand a row to see each point.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>Not modelled:</b> race physics (actual lap times) and effects that are pure game logic (e.g. "start with Surge"), which only show
    as text.
  </p>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  .planner-notes {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    max-width: 90ch;
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 13.5px;

    p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    b {
      color: var(--color-fg);
    }
  }
</style>
